● v0.7.0 INT8 quantization infrastructure is complete. Here's the summary:

  v0.7.0 INT8 Quantization Implementation

  New Files

  - python/kpu/quantization.py - Core quantization module with:
    - QuantDtype enum - All quantization types (INT8, FP16, BF16, FP8 variants, INT4, FP4)
    - QuantizationConfig - Configuration for quantized tensors
    - compute_scale_zero_point() - Calibration utility
    - compute_per_channel_params() - Per-channel calibration
    - quantize() / dequantize() - Core Q/DQ operations
    - quantized_matmul_int8() - INT8 matrix multiplication
    - quantized_linear_int8() - INT8 linear layer
    - calculate_matmul_traffic() - Memory traffic calculation
    - bandwidth_reduction_factor() - Bandwidth reduction metric

  Modified Files

  - python/kpu/dfx_emitter.py - Added:
    - Extended DFXDataType with FP8, INT4 types
    - Added bytes_per_element property
    - New opcodes: QUANTIZE, DEQUANTIZE, QUANTIZED_MATMUL, etc.
  - python/kpu/__init__.py - Exports all quantization APIs
  - docs/plans/v0.7-quantization-gap-analysis.md - Updated with fast bfloat16 notes

  Test Results
  ┌──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────┐
  │           Test           │        Result        │
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
  │ Quantize/Dequantize      │ 0.4% max error       │
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
  │ INT8 MatMul accuracy     │ 1.03% relative error │
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
  │ Memory reduction         │ 4.0x (INT8 vs FP32)  │
  ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
  │ Per-channel quantization │ Working              │
  └──────────────────────────┴──────────────────────┘
  Version

  - Updated to v0.7.0 in __init__.py and pyproject.toml

  Would you like me to:
  1. Create a CHANGELOG entry and commit this work?
  2. Continue to v0.7.1 (FP16 support)?
  3. Add more INT8 tests or examples?


● v0.7.1 has been released:

  Commit: 8c578bd - Add FP16 support (v0.7.1)

  Tag: v0.7.1 pushed to origin

  New FP16 APIs:
  ┌──────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │       Function       │              Description               │
  ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ kpu.fp16_matmul()    │ Half-precision matrix multiplication   │
  ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ kpu.fp16_linear()    │ FP16 linear layer (y = x @ W.T + bias) │
  ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ kpu.fp16_conv2d()    │ FP16 2D convolution                    │
  ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ kpu.cast_to_fp16()   │ Convert tensor to float16              │
  ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ kpu.cast_from_fp16() │ Convert tensor back to float32         │
  ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ kpu.fp16_range()     │ Returns (±65504)                       │
  ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ kpu.fp16_precision() │ Returns machine epsilon (~9.77e-04)    │
  └──────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────┘
  Test Results:
  - FP16 matmul relative error: ~0.15%
  - FP16 linear relative error: ~0.33%
  - Memory bandwidth reduction: 2x vs FP32

  Next: v0.7.2 (BF16 support using fast bfloat16 from Universal)

